# Local install and build artifacts.
node_modules/
.npm-cache/
.pnpm-store/
.live-cache/
.test-cache/
pnpm-lock.yaml
# package-lock.json is committed on purpose: the test suites build the
# harness's own BlockAssembler from @deepseek-ai/dsh-llm, so the contract
# they check is only meaningful against the version that was verified.
*.log
# Launch kit and working notes: local to this checkout, never published and
# never part of the plugin. The screenshot instructions moved in here with
# them; the images themselves belong in assets/, which git picks up once they
# exist. Git cannot track an empty directory, so assets/ needs no entry here —
# and an entry would defeat the point, since a screenshot the market is meant
# to show has to be committed.
promotion/
# The IDE's own project directory: per machine, per developer, and full of state
# that only means anything to the person who generated it. It sits here rather
# than in the group above because, unlike the working notes, it appears the
# moment anyone opens the project in a JetBrains IDE — so leaving it untracked is
# what stops a commit from carrying a stranger's window layout. Team-wide
# settings belong in a committed .editorconfig instead.
.idea/
# A local orientation note: this checkout's paths, the current check count, and
# the rules a change tends to run into. It goes stale on every commit, and the
# committed README, docs/ and CHANGELOG are the facts that ship — so it stays
# out of the history rather than in it. The name is the ecosystem's convention,
# which is also why a tool may read it without being asked.
AGENTS.md
